  "summary": "The AI detection tool Pangram flags 99 percent of a prize-winning Peruvian novel as AI-generated, but Mexican publisher Almadía is standing by the award after its own review. Pangram also classified over 80 percent of the author's personal texts as machine-written. French publisher Gallimard plans to start screening manuscripts with the tool. The article Pangram flags 99 percent of an award-winning Peruvian novel as AI-generated, but the publisher stands by its author appeared first on The Decoder .",
